<Docs title="API reference" active="API reference">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">REFERENCE / 04</span><h1>API reference</h1><p>Stable shapes for decisions, delegation, audit, and integrations.</p></div>
  <h2>AuthZEN decision request</h2><div class="doc-code">POST /access/v1/evaluation<br /><br />&#123;<br />  "subject": &#123; "type": "Agent", "id": "support-copilot" &#125;,<br />  "action": &#123; "type": "Action", "id": "tickets.read" &#125;,<br />  "resource": &#123; "type": "Ticket", "id": "4420" &#125;<br />&#125;</div>
  <h2>Decision response</h2><div class="doc-code">&#123;<br />  "decision": true,<br />  "reason": "Example: matching permit"<br />&#125;</div>
  <p>This illustrative Ticket request requires your own schema and policy. The starter schema uses actions such as ToolCall::repo_read and resources such as Repository. Every entity reference uses a case-sensitive type and id. Optional context contains policy facts; optional entities supplies Cedar attributes and hierarchy.</p>
  <h2>Batch evaluation</h2><p>POST /access/v1/evaluations accepts an evaluations array of up to 100 single requests. evaluation_semantics may be execute_all, deny_on_first_deny, or permit_on_first_permit. The response contains an evaluations array of boolean decisions.</p>
  <h2>Handling responses</h2><p>Execute a tool only when the response succeeds and decision is true. A false decision is an authorization denial. Authentication failures, malformed requests, timeouts, and unreachable servers must not be interpreted as permission to proceed.</p>
  <h2>SDKs and examples</h2><p>The TypeScript Client wraps the installed agentguard CLI using a synchronous child process. It requires Node.js and the CLI binary; it is not a browser client. Client.check raises AuthorizationDenied when authorization fails. The Strands example uses an HTTP intervention hook. Rust consumers can call the core engine or mount the router.</p><p>See the <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/tree/master/typescript/agentguard">TypeScript source</a>, <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/tree/master/examples">integration examples</a>, and <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/crates/agentguard-server/proto/agentguard.proto">gRPC protocol definition</a>.</p>
  <h2>Useful commands</h2><div class="docs-table"><div><b>agentguard validate</b><span>Validate schema and policies.</span></div><div><b>agentguard sim</b><span>Evaluate a request without executing it.</span></div><div><b>agentguard audit</b><span>Inspect and verify the decision chain.</span></div><div><b>agentguard delegate</b><span>Issue a scoped delegation token.</span></div></div>
</Docs>
